A revision now replies to the first version of its series, but the
series posted before that convention are still a chain of top-level
threads, one per version, joined only by the "Link to v(N-1)" line
in each cover letter. Reading the history of any of them means
following those links by hand, one thread at a time, and its review
is scattered across all of them.

rethread.py follows the links back to the first version and rewrites
the threading headers of each older revision, so the list as it
stands reads the same way as the series posted from now on. On the
list today it moves 123 messages and folds 147 threads into 103. It
changes only In-Reply-To and References, and a rerun changes
nothing.
