    jj commit -m "mail: Thread each revision under its first version"
    notmuch dump > /tmp/notmuch.tags
    rm -rf <your database's xapian directory>
    notmuch new
    notmuch restore < /tmp/notmuch.tags

Testing: on a copy of the list, --apply rewrites 123 files and a
second dry run plans nothing. Every changed line is an In-Reply-To
or References header. A fresh notmuch database on the copy shows 103
threads where there were 147; the signoz port is one 42-message
thread with v2 to v10 under v1. Reindexing the changed messages in
the old database only reached 119, since it leaves replies in their
old threads, while dump, rebuild, and restore reached 103 and kept a
tag set by hand.

